<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Paz</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nuestra Señora de La Paz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Paz is a city in the Andes of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, founded by the Spanish in 1548 and today the seat of Bolivia's government. Its uprising of July 1809, following that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sucre">Chuquisaca</a>, was among the first movements towards independence in Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. Sucre remains the constitutional capital, while the executive and legislature sit in La Paz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-paz.jpg" alt="La Paz" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Parallelepiped09 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_del_centro_de_La_Paz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
